    {
      "id": "6o6wswp",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "11.1 Introduction to Computer Networks"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Computer networks enable resource sharing, communication, and centralized data management across connected nodes.",
        "Networks are classified by geographical scale into Local Area Network (LAN), Metropolitan Area Network (MAN), and Wide Area Network (WAN).",
        "Essential network devices include Routers (path determination across networks), Switches (intelligent intra-network packet delivery), Hubs (broadcasting devices), and Modems (signal conversion).",
        "Network topologies represent physical or logical layouts: Bus, Star, Ring, Mesh, and Tree.",
        "Mesh topology offers maximum redundancy and fault tolerance at the cost of high cabling complexity."
      ],
      "id": "q9topag"
    },
