    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Hub is a physical layer (Layer 1) device that broadcasts data to all ports, whereas Switch is a data link layer (Layer 2) device that unicasts data to specific target ports.",
        "The total number of physical connections required in a fully connected mesh network with 'n' devices is n(n-1)/2.",
        "Modem performs Modulation (Digital to Analog) and Demodulation (Analog to Digital) for telephone line transmission.",
        "Star Topology relies on a central hub/switch; if the central node fails, the entire network goes down."
      ],
